{"timestamp": 1779354276.2038755, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 13, "data": {"caller": "player_0", "reason": "Alice reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Bob"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779354276.2048123, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 13, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779354286.5165124, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I found Bob's body in Medbay. My route was Storage -> Lower Engine -> Upper Engine -> Medbay. \n\nHere is the most important piece of information: when I was in Upper Engine around tick 9, I saw Eve enter Upper Engine coming directly *from* Medbay. She was still in Upper Engine with me until tick 11 before I headed into Medbay and found the body. \n\nEve, you were just in the room where Bob died right before I got there. Care to explain? I'd like everyone to hear Eve's defense before we vote, but she is highly suspicious right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1779354299.857469, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route this round was entirely on the left side of the ship. I started in Upper Engine, went up to Oxygen, came back through Upper Engine, then moved down to Lower Engine, and finally ended up in Storage where I was doing a task when the meeting was called. \n\nThe interesting part is that I didn't see a single soul my entire route. I must have passed through Upper Engine and Lower Engine well before Alice and Eve got there. Since I saw literally no one, it makes sense that everyone else, including the killer, was congregating around the middle or right side of the map.\n\nAlice's accusation is extremely specific and very damning. If Eve was walking out of Medbay right before Alice walked in and found Bob, that's almost a smoking gun. I'm definitely leaning towards voting Eve based on this, but like Alice said, let's hear Eve's defense first. If anyone else was near Medbay or Upper Engine and can corroborate or debunk Alice's timeline, please speak up!"}}
{"timestamp": 1779354312.0496554, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I can actually back up Alice's timeline perfectly here, which looks really bad for Eve. \n\nMy route this round was Electrical, then Medbay, down to Storage, and finally over to Navigation where I was when the meeting was called. \n\nHere is the crucial piece of information: at tick 7, I saw Bob leaving Storage and heading directly into Medbay. \n\nIf Bob walked into Medbay at T7, and Alice saw Eve leaving Medbay at T9 right before finding his body, the timeline is airtight. Eve must have killed Bob right after he walked in. Alice's story completely matches Bob's last known movements. \n\nEve, I'm looking forward to hearing your defense, but this timeline is extremely damning. Unless Frank or Eve has some ground-breaking information to contradict this, I'm fully confident in voting Eve today."}}
{"timestamp": 1779354331.9827557, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "This is a complete misunderstanding of the timeline, and the math actually proves I'm innocent. Please listen carefully!\n\nMy route was exactly: Cafeteria -> Electrical -> Medbay -> Upper Engine. \n\nI arrived in Upper Engine at tick 9, where I saw Alice. Because it takes 2 ticks to travel from Medbay to Upper Engine, that means I *left* Medbay at tick 7. \n\nNow, let's look at Diana's statement. Diana said she saw Bob leaving Storage and heading to Medbay at tick 7. The travel time from Storage to Medbay is ALSO 2 ticks. That means Bob wouldn't have even arrived in Medbay until tick 9! \n\nBy the time Bob stepped foot into Medbay at T9, I was already in Upper Engine standing right next to Alice. I never even crossed paths with Bob, and I certainly didn't see his body because he wasn't even there yet when I passed through. \n\nAlice, I saw you leave Upper Engine to head down to Medbay at T11. If Bob arrived at T9, he was in there for a couple of ticks before you walked in. Since I am 100% innocent and the timeline proves I physically could not have killed him, the killer has to be whoever else was around Medbay, or someone who can't account for their whereabouts between T9 and T13.\n\nFrank, you're the last to speak. Where were you during all of this? Because right now, the math clears me completely. I think we should wait to hear from Frank before making any rash decisions."}}
{"timestamp": 1779354357.9373224, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I can actually confirm the very beginning of Charlie's route. Charlie, you said you didn't see anyone, but I actually saw you enter Oxygen from Upper Engine right at tick 1 just as I was leaving. I headed straight across to Cafeteria, then spent the rest of the round doing tasks on the right side of the ship in Weapons, Security, and Electrical. I only just looped back around to Upper Engine at the very end of the round, totally bypassing Medbay.\n\nEve, your math defense is clever, but it relies heavily on the assumption that everyone moved instantly without stopping for a single tick. Between Diana seeing Bob head exactly to Medbay, and Alice physically seeing you leave that exact room right before finding the body, the eyewitness testimony is just way too strong to ignore. It\u2019s much more likely you killed him right as he walked in and fled before Alice arrived. \n\nI'm trusting Alice and Diana's corroborated timeline here. I'm voting Eve.\n\nEve"}}
